$ =====================================================================
$ RBE3 TEST SERIES -- Deck 04: PARTIAL DEPENDENCY (translations only)
$
$ Exercises a different valid RBE3 configuration (not a bug case):
$ REFC=123 only, so the reference grid's rotations are NOT part of
$ this RBE3 at all (left free/governed elsewhere). This is the
$ classic "distribute a load / average a displacement over a patch
$ of grids" usage, with no rigid-rotation fitting involved --
$ REFC=123 means CDOF_D(4),(5),(6) are all '0', so the code never
$ writes the rotation-coupling terms (DX_BAR/DY_BAR/DZ_BAR) for this
$ RBE3 at all. The dependent translation is then a PURE weighted
$ average of the independent grids' translations:
$   U_D = sum(Wi*Ui) / sum(Wi)
$
$ Three independent grids, uniform per-grid weights (1.0, 3.0, 2.0),
$ arbitrary (non-rigid-body) prescribed translations -- there's no
$ rigid-body-recovery property to check here since rotations aren't
$ involved; this is a plain sanity check of the weighted-average
$ arithmetic itself.
$
$ Expected result, grid 700:
$   T1 = 0.150000   T2 = 0.033333   T3 = 0.158333
$ (= [1.0*(.10,.20,.30) + 3.0*(.40,-.10,.05) + 2.0*(-.20,.15,.25)] / 6.0)
$
$ Both the current (buggy) and a corrected RBE3_PROC.f90 should give
$ this exact answer -- confirms the weighted-average machinery itself
$ (WT6, WRITE_L1J_123) is independent of, and unaffected by, either
$ of the two known bugs.
$ =====================================================================
SOL 101
CEND
DISP = ALL
SPC = 1
BEGIN BULK
$
GRID,700,,0.,0.,0.
$
GRID,701,,2.0,0.0,0.0
GRID,702,,0.0,2.0,0.0
GRID,703,,-2.0,-1.0,0.0
$
GRID,600,,5.,5.,5.
GRID,601,,6.,5.,5.
MAT1,1,1.,,0.
PROD,1,1,1.
CROD,97,1,600,601
$
$ REFC = 123 only -- rotations of grid 700 are not dependent here.
RBE3    20              700     123     1.0     123     701     3.0     +A1
+A1     123     702     2.0     123     703
$
SPC,1,701,1,0.10
SPC,1,701,2,0.20
SPC,1,701,3,0.30
SPC,1,701,456,0.
$
SPC,1,702,1,0.40
SPC,1,702,2,-0.10
SPC,1,702,3,0.05
SPC,1,702,456,0.
$
SPC,1,703,1,-0.20
SPC,1,703,2,0.15
SPC,1,703,3,0.25
SPC,1,703,456,0.
$
$ Grid 700's rotations aren't part of this RBE3 -- fix them
$ externally so the model is well posed.
SPC,1,700,456,0.
$
SPC,1,600,123456,0.
$ (grid 601 deliberately left unconstrained -- gives the model a
$  genuine free DOF so MSC Nastran has an L-set to solve; it's an
$  unloaded dummy CROD end, disconnected from the RBE3 under test, so
$  this has no effect on the RBE3 results.)
$
ENDDATA
